Spec: specs/000-foundation/spec.md (AC5, AC8, AC11); ADR 0002; research Q3, Q4, Q5
Why this approach: the yaml.Node walk gives key lines, unknown and duplicate keys, and type checks without touching values; the KnownFields decoder on the raw bytes stays as the spec's backstop; values are validated by our own functions, so no parser message reaches an Error.
Trade-off / known limit: yaml.v3's syntax-error line is sometimes the line before the bad one (Q4), passed through as is. An unreadable default config.yaml is an error, not defaults (Q5). Null values keep the default (Q3).
Verified by: GOFLAGS=-count=1 make verify; TestDefaults, TestLoad_UnknownKey, TestLoad_ErrorsNeverContainValue (17 cases, every reason in steps 1-5, including the reachable invalid config path), TestLoad_MalformedYAMLReportsLine, TestLoad_EmptyFile, TestLoad_ExampleFileIsDefaults, TestLoad_InvalidDuration, TestLoad_InvalidAddress, plus TestLoad_FileLookup, TestLoad_Precedence, TestSettingsCoverFileKeys.
